-   name: framer
    id: epy_block
    parameters:
        _source_code: "r\"\"\"\nContinuous-stream PDU framer for GNU Radio (TX side).\n\
            \nReplaces this chain from the original flowgraph:\n    PDU to Tagged\
            \ Stream -> Stream CRC32 -> Protocol Formatter -> Tagged Stream Mux\n\
            \    (+ preamble/postamble Vector Sources + Stream to Tagged Stream x2)\
            \ -> Tag Gate\nand the first half of the Constellation Modulator (unpack\
            \ bits -> Gray map ->\ndifferential encode). Output = differentially encoded\
            \ SYMBOL INDICES, followed in the\nflowgraph by \"Chunks to Symbols\"\
            \ -> RRC \"Polyphase Arbitrary Resampler\" -> gain.\n\nWhy symbols and\
            \ not bytes: GNU Radio buffers are sized in ITEMS. One byte at a framer\n\
            output is 32 samples of airtime (BPSK, sps=4) so a 4096-byte buffer alone\
            \ delays every\nframe by 131k samples; a symbol is only 4 samples. Measured\
            \ one-way TX latency at\n1 Msps went from ~700 ms (byte framer + Constellation\
            \ Modulator) to a few ms.\n\nWhy:\n  1. The PlutoSDR Sink only pushes\
            \ a buffer to the radio when it is FULL. With bursty\n     tagged-stream\
            \ TX, the last packet of a burst sits in a half-full buffer until the\n\
            \     next packet arrives -> ACKs/last chunks get \"stuck\" -> spurious\
            \ ARQ timeouts.\n     This block NEVER starves: when there is no packet\
            \ to send it emits idle bytes,\n     so the radio transmits continuously\
            \ and every packet leaves immediately.\n  2. Continuous TX keeps the receiver's\
            \ Symbol Sync and Costas loop locked all the\n     time, so a 1024-byte\
            \ preamble is no longer needed (it was ~60% of airtime).\n  3. Downstream\
            \ back-pressure from the PlutoSDR Sink paces this block at exactly the\n\
            \     air rate - no time.sleep() pacing tricks are needed for the radio.\n\
            \nFrame format (bit-exact with the stock RX blocks\n\"Correlate Access\
            \ Code - Tag Stream\" + \"Stream CRC32 (check, packed)\"):\n\n    [preamble\
            \ 0x55..] [access code 8B] [len 2B BE] [len 2B BE] [payload] [CRC32 4B\
            \ LE] [postamble]\n                                        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\
            \ len = len(payload)+4\n                                             \
            \                  \\_____ whitened _____/\n\nWhitening: payload+CRC are\
            \ XORed with the keystream of GNU Radio's\n\"Additive Scrambler\" (mask\
            \ 0x8A, seed 0x7F, length 7, 8 bits/byte, reset on every\npacket). Without\
            \ it, long runs of identical bytes (WAV silence, flat image areas,\nzero\
            \ padding) give the receiver's Symbol Sync / Costas loop no transitions;\
            \ those\nframes then fail CRC on EVERY retry and ARQ cannot recover. The\
            \ RX flowgraph undoes it\nwith an Additive Scrambler block (same params,\
            \ Reset Tag Key = packet_len) placed\nbetween Repack Bits and Stream CRC32.\n\
            \nQuiet FDD (idle_silence=True with burst_preamble_len): the radio keeps\
            \ sending idle symbols\nfor `hangover` symbols after a DATA frame (none\
            \ after an ACK / beacon) (so back-to-back frames need only the short preamble),\n\
            then goes SILENT. A frame that starts after silence gets the long burst\
            \ preamble so the far\nreceiver's AGC / Symbol Sync / Costas re-lock.\
            \ Why: an E200 whose own continuous\ntransmitter desensitises its receiver\
            \ is deaf all the time in continuous FDD (the direction\nINTO that radio\
            \ crawls), but only during its own short ACK bursts in quiet FDD.\n\n\
            Priority: frames whose first two bytes are (MAGIC, type != DATA) - i.e.\
            \ ARQ ACKs and\nbeacons from transport.py - jump ahead of queued DATA\
            \ frames. This keeps ACK latency\nlow even when this node is simultaneously\
            \ sending a large file (full duplex).\n\"\"\"\nimport collections\nimport\
            \ struct\nimport zlib\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport pmt\nfrom gnuradio\
            \ import gr\n\nDEFAULT_ACCESS_CODE = \"1010110011011101101001001110001011110010100011000010000011111100\"\
            \n\nSCRAMBLER_MASK, SCRAMBLER_SEED, SCRAMBLER_LEN = 0x8A, 0x7F, 7\n\n\n\
            def scrambler_keystream(n, mask=SCRAMBLER_MASK, seed=SCRAMBLER_SEED, reg_len=SCRAMBLER_LEN):\n\
            \    \"\"\"Byte keystream identical to digital.additive_scrambler_bb(mask,\
            \ seed, len, 0, 8).\"\"\"\n    sr, out = seed, bytearray()\n    for _\
            \ in range(n):\n        b = 0\n        for i in range(8):\n          \
            \  b |= (sr & 1) << i\n            newbit = bin(sr & mask).count(\"1\"\
            ) & 1\n            sr = (sr >> 1) | (newbit << reg_len)\n        out.append(b)\n\
            \    return np.frombuffer(bytes(out), dtype=np.uint8)\n\n\n# Must match\
            \ transport.py\nMAGIC = 0xA5\nTYPE_DATA = 0x01\n\n\nclass blk(gr.sync_block):\n\
            \    \"\"\"PDU Framer (continuous). Message input 'in' (PDU of uint8),\
            \ byte stream output.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, access_code=DEFAULT_ACCESS_CODE,\
            \ preamble_len=4, postamble_len=2,\n                 max_queue=2048, idle_seed=1234,\
            \ bits_per_symbol=1, pre_diff_code=(),\n                 idle_silence=False,\
            \ burst_preamble_len=0, hangover=0):\n        gr.sync_block.__init__(self,\
            \ name=\"PDU Framer (continuous)\",\n                               in_sig=None,\
            \ out_sig=[np.uint8])\n        self.message_port_register_in(pmt.intern(\"\
            in\"))\n        self.set_msg_handler(pmt.intern(\"in\"), self._on_pdu)\n\
            \n        ac_int = int(access_code, 2)\n        self._ac = ac_int.to_bytes(len(access_code)\
            \ // 8, \"big\")\n        self._pre = b\"\\x55\" * int(preamble_len)\n\
            \        self._post = b\"\\x55\" * int(postamble_len)\n        self._max_queue\
            \ = int(max_queue)\n        self._ks = scrambler_keystream(0x1000)\n \
            \       self._q_hi = collections.deque()   # ACK / control\n        self._q_lo\
            \ = collections.deque()   # DATA\n        self._cur = np.zeros(0, dtype=np.uint8)\n\
            \        self._pos = 0\n        # Pseudo-random idle fill: keeps plenty\
            \ of symbol transitions for timing\n        # recovery and a flat spectrum.\
            \ A false access-code match inside idle data is\n        # rejected by\
            \ the duplicated length field + CRC32.\n        self._k = int(bits_per_symbol)\n\
            \        self._M = 1 << self._k\n        # TDD mode: between frames output\
            \ symbol index M, which the flowgraph's\n        # Chunks to Symbols table\
            \ maps to 0+0j -> the radio is SILENT when it has\n        # nothing to\
            \ send (no self-interference into its own receiver), while the\n     \
            \   # sample stream to the PlutoSDR Sink stays continuous (no stuck buffers).\n\
            \        self._silence = bool(idle_silence)\n        self.SILENCE = self._M\n\
            \        # quiet FDD: idle symbols for `hangover` symbols after a frame,\
            \ then silence; a frame\n        # starting after silence is preceded\
            \ by extra preamble (burst_preamble_len in total)\n        extra = max(0,\
            \ int(burst_preamble_len) - int(preamble_len)) if idle_silence else 0\n\
            \        self._hang = int(hangover) if extra else 0\n        self._idle_n\
            \ = 0\n        self._quiet = True              # nothing transmitted yet\n\
            \        self._after_data = False        # hangover only after DATA (an\
            \ ACK goes silent at once)\n        self.bursts = 0\n        code = list(pre_diff_code)\
            \ if len(pre_diff_code) else list(range(self._M))\n        self._map =\
            \ np.array(code, dtype=np.uint8)\n        self._weights = (1 << np.arange(self._k\
            \ - 1, -1, -1)).astype(np.uint8)\n        # Burst preamble: 0x55 then\
            \ FIXED pseudo-random bytes. After differential encoding a long\n    \
            \    # 0x55 run is a periodic ++--++-- pattern on which the symbol-timing\
            \ loop can settle half a\n        # symbol off; random symbols have no\
            \ such false lock point (simulation: frames sent alone\n        # after\
            \ silence decode ~80% instead of ~50%).\n        if extra:\n         \
            \   rnd = np.random.default_rng(20260).integers(0, 256, max(0, extra -\
            \ 4), dtype=np.uint8).tobytes()\n            self._extra_pre = self._to_chunks((b\"\
            \\x55\" * 4 + rnd)[:extra])\n        else:\n            self._extra_pre\
            \ = None\n        self._diff_state = 0\n        rng = np.random.default_rng(int(idle_seed))\n\
            \        self._idle = rng.integers(0, self._M, 1 << 16, dtype=np.uint8)\n\
            \        self._idle_pos = 0\n        self.dropped = 0\n        self.sent\
            \ = 0\n        # Keep the byte buffer after this block small so a newly\
            \ queued frame does not\n        # wait behind a large backlog of idle\
            \ bytes (lower RTT for the ARQ).\n        try:\n            self.set_max_output_buffer(0,\
            \ 4096)\n        except Exception:\n            pass\n\n    def _to_chunks(self,\
            \ b):\n        \"\"\"bytes -> k-bit symbol values, MSB first (same as\
            \ Packed to Unpacked, MSB).\"\"\"\n        bits = np.unpackbits(np.frombuffer(b,\
            \ dtype=np.uint8) if isinstance(b, bytes) else b)\n        if self._k\
            \ == 1:\n            return bits\n        return (bits.reshape(-1, self._k)\
            \ * self._weights).sum(axis=1).astype(np.uint8)\n\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\
            \ messages\n    def _on_pdu(self, msg):\n        if not pmt.is_pair(msg):\n\
            \            return\n        vec = pmt.cdr(msg)\n        if not pmt.is_u8vector(vec):\n\
            \            return\n        payload = bytes(pmt.u8vector_elements(vec))\n\
            \        n = len(payload)\n        if n == 0 or n + 4 > 0x0FFF:\n    \
            \        return\n        ln = struct.pack(\">H\", n + 4)\n        body\
            \ = np.frombuffer(payload + struct.pack(\"<I\", zlib.crc32(payload) &\
            \ 0xFFFFFFFF),\n                             dtype=np.uint8) ^ self._ks[:n\
            \ + 4]\n        arr = self._to_chunks(np.concatenate((\n            np.frombuffer(self._pre\
            \ + self._ac + ln + ln, dtype=np.uint8),\n            body, np.frombuffer(self._post,\
            \ dtype=np.uint8))))\n        is_ctrl = n >= 2 and payload[0] == MAGIC\
            \ and payload[1] != TYPE_DATA\n        q = self._q_hi if is_ctrl else\
            \ self._q_lo\n        if len(q) >= self._max_queue:\n            self.dropped\
            \ += 1          # ARQ will recover it\n            return\n        q.append(arr)\n\
            \n    def _next_frame(self):\n        if self._q_hi:\n            self._after_data\
            \ = False\n            return self._q_hi.popleft()\n        if self._q_lo:\n\
            \            self._after_data = True\n            return self._q_lo.popleft()\n\
            \        return None\n\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\
            \ stream\n    def work(self, input_items, output_items):\n        out\
            \ = output_items[0]\n        n = len(out)\n        i = 0\n        while\
            \ i < n:\n            if self._pos >= len(self._cur):\n              \
            \  f = self._next_frame()\n                if f is None:\n           \
            \         break\n                if self._extra_pre is not None and self._quiet:\
            \   # first frame after silence\n                    f = np.concatenate((self._extra_pre,\
            \ f))\n                    self.bursts += 1\n                self._quiet,\
            \ self._idle_n = False, 0\n                self._cur, self._pos = f, 0\n\
            \                self.sent += 1\n            take = min(n - i, len(self._cur)\
            \ - self._pos)\n            out[i:i + take] = self._cur[self._pos:self._pos\
            \ + take]\n            i += take\n            self._pos += take\n    \
            \    n_data = i\n        if i < n:\n            take = min(n - i, 512)\n\
            \            hang = min(take, max(0, self._hang - self._idle_n)) if self._silence\
            \ and self._after_data else 0\n            if hang:            # quiet\
            \ FDD hangover: idle symbols, then silence\n                idx = (self._idle_pos\
            \ + np.arange(hang)) & 0xFFFF\n                out[i:i + hang] = self._idle[idx]\n\
            \                self._idle_pos = (self._idle_pos + hang) & 0xFFFF\n \
            \               self._idle_n += hang\n                n_data = i + hang\n\
            \                i += hang\n                take -= hang\n           \
            \ if take <= 0:\n                pass\n            elif self._silence:\n\
            \                out[i:i + take] = self.SILENCE\n                self._quiet\
            \ = True\n            else:\n                # Idle fill (random symbols):\
            \ keeps the radio transmitting continuously\n                # so every\
            \ frame leaves immediately and the RX loops stay locked.\n           \
            \     idx = (self._idle_pos + np.arange(take)) & 0xFFFF\n            \
            \    out[i:i + take] = self._idle[idx]\n                n_data = i + take\n\
            \            i += take\n        if n_data:\n            # Gray pre-diff\
            \ map + differential encoding: y[n] = (x[n] + y[n-1]) mod M\n        \
            \    seg = self._map[out[:n_data]].astype(np.int64)\n            seg[0]\
            \ += self._diff_state\n            enc = np.cumsum(seg) % self._M\n  \
            \          out[:n_data] = enc\n            self._diff_state = int(enc[-1])\n\
            \        return i\n"
        access_code: access_code
        affinity: ''
        alias: ''
        bits_per_symbol: '1'
        burst_preamble_len: 128 if duplex == 'fdd' else 0
        comment: ''
        hangover: 2048 if duplex == 'fdd' else 0
        idle_seed: '1234'
        idle_silence: duplex != 'fdd-cont'
        max_queue: '2048'
        maxoutbuf: '0'
        minoutbuf: '0'
        postamble_len: '2'
        pre_diff_code: '[]'
        preamble_len: 64 if duplex == 'tdd' else 4
    states:
        _io_cache: ('PDU Framer (continuous)', 'blk', [('access_code', "'1010110011011101101001001110001011110010100011000010000011111100'"),
            ('preamble_len', '4'), ('postamble_len', '2'), ('max_queue', '2048'),
            ('idle_seed', '1234'), ('bits_per_symbol', '1'), ('pre_diff_code', '()'),
            ('idle_silence', 'False'), ('burst_preamble_len', '0'), ('hangover', '0')],
            [('in', 'message', 1)], [('0', 'byte', 1)], "PDU Framer (continuous).
            Message input 'in' (PDU of uint8), byte stream output.", [])
        bus_sink: false
        bus_source: false
        bus_structure: null
        coordinate:
        - 230
        - 300
        state: enabled
-   name: note_rx
    id: note
    parameters:
        alias: ''
        comment: ''
        note: 'RX: Pluto -> look-ahead AGC (C++ blocks) -> RRC -> Symbol Sync -> Costas
            -> Decoder -> Diff Dec -> Map -> Unpack -> Correlate AC -> Repack (MSB)
            -> Descramble -> CRC32 check -> PDU'
    states:
        bus_sink: false
        bus_source: false
        bus_structure: null
        coordinate:
        - 10
        - 520
        state: enabled
-   name: note_tx
    id: note
    parameters:
        alias: ''
        comment: ''
        note: 'TX: Socket PDU -> Framer (framing+CRC+whitening+Gray+diff-enc, emits
            symbols; index M = silence when idle in fdd / tdd) -> Chunks to Symbols
            (+0j entry) -> RRC x sps -> gain -> Pluto'
    states:
        bus_sink: false
        bus_source: false
        bus_structure: null
        coordinate:
        - 10
        - 260
        state: enabled
-   name: note_vars
    id: note
    parameters:
        alias: ''
        comment: ''
        note: 'node = 1 or 2 (node 1 TX f1 / RX f2, node 2 the opposite). duplex =
            ''fdd'' (default: silent when idle), ''fdd-cont'' (idle symbols all the
            time) or ''tdd''; must match app.py --duplex. f1 / f2 must match the app''s
            F1 / F2. samp_rate 4000000 + sps 4 = --profile robust, 2000000 + sps 2
            = lean, 10000000 + sps 4 = balanced'
    states:
        bus_sink: false
        bus_source: false
        bus_structure: null
        coordinate:
        - 10
        - 100
        state: enabled
